  "@@locale": "en",
  "holdemRulesSummary": "No-Limit Texas hold'em between players, 6 seats: no rake, no powers, the whole pot goes to the winners. The bots' stacks belong to the house.",
  "holdemRulesBlinds": "Blinds per tier: $1/$2, $5/$10 or $25/$50 (unit: $1). Buy-in 40 to 100 big blinds, debited when you sit down; rebuy between hands, up to 100 big blinds. Your stack is credited back when you leave — at the end of the hand if you are in it.",
  "holdemRulesButton": "The button moves one seat each hand (moving big blind). Heads-up, the button posts the small blind, acts first before the flop and last after it. A newcomer waits for the big blind to reach their seat before being dealt in.",
  "holdemRulesBetting": "No-Limit: the minimum bet is one big blind; a raise must be at least the last full bet or raise of the street. The slider shows the total amount \"to\" (raise to $60).",
  "holdemRulesAllIn": "You may go all-in at any time, even for less than a minimum raise. An incomplete all-in does not reopen the betting: players who already acted may only call or fold.",
  "holdemRulesPots": "When an all-in player cannot cover a bet, a side pot is formed: they can only win the pots they put chips in. The part of a bet nobody called goes back to its owner.",
  "holdemRulesShowdown": "Automatic showdown: the best 5-card hand from your 2 cards and the 5 board cards. A split pot is divided in whole dollars, the odd dollar going to the first winner after the button. If everyone folds, the last player takes the pot without showing.",
  "holdemRulesTimeouts": "20 s per decision: on timeout you check if possible, otherwise your hand is folded. Two timeouts in a row put you away; away (or out of chips) for 3 hands, your stack is credited back and your seat freed.",
  "holdemRulesMarkets": "Spectator markets on each hand: \"An ace on the board?\" and \"3 or more cards of one suit on the board?\". They close at the flop and settle on the board fixed at the deal, even if everyone folds before.",
  "holdemRulesFairness": "Deliberate choice: the deck is fixed at the deal by the committed seed (its SHA-256 is published beforehand). The seed revealed after the hand makes every card verifiable — folded hands included, which are therefore visible to everyone (\"Last hand\" button).",
